/-!
# Strong Kadison–Kastler stability

The theorem `KadisonKastler.universal_strong_stability` gives one positive
tolerance for all complex Hilbert spaces and represented unital von Neumann
algebras, in terms of the desired displacement of a conjugating unitary.

The proof combines finite-factor estimates, modular preparation, regular-core
descent, two-ratio product absorption, and reduction to arbitrary
representations. State homogeneity of the product follows from a uniform
projection-gap contraction and positive representatives. Its expected matrix
subfactor is constructed in the original representation.
-/
